      <span class="eyebrow">Our team</span>
      <h2>Founded from <em>first-hand experience</em>.</h2>
      <p class="body">Qualiber was founded from first-hand experience of the problem it is trying to solve. Built by someone who has lived that complexity as a practitioner and user, not just observed it from the outside.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bio">
      <div class="person">
      <h3 class="person-name">Karthik S.</h3>
      <p class="person-role">Founder and CEO</p>
      <p>Karthik S. is the Founder and CEO of Qualiber, bringing nearly two decades of experience in quality engineering, technical program management, and software delivery. With a career spanning Amazon and Apple, he combines deep technical expertise with experience leading complex, cross-functional programs at scale.</p>
      <p>Prior to founding Qualiber, Karthik led end-to-end quality and release strategy for Amazon’s reading platforms, serving more than 50 million users. During his four years at Amazon, he developed a GenAI-powered testing accelerator that reduced execution time by 50% and delivered $1.2 million in annual run-rate savings. He also took GenAI and agentic AI initiatives from pilot through production adoption and served as an Amazon Bar Raiser, contributing to hiring standards across the organisation.</p>
      <p>Previously, Karthik directed quality engineering and testing for Apple News, where his work included improving publisher-payout data accuracy and developing machine-learning-driven approaches to detect anomalies across analytics systems.</p>
      <p>Karthik’s experience across large-scale technology environments has reinforced a central principle behind his work: successful software delivery depends not only on technical capability, but also on effective coordination and evidence-based decision-making. He brings this perspective to Qualiber, where he is building an AI-powered decision platform designed to give engineering teams clearer, evidence-based insight into release readiness.</p>
      <p>Karthik holds an Executive MBA from the University of Chicago Booth School of Business and a Bachelor of Engineering in Electrical, Electronics and Communications Engineering from Anna University Chennai.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="person">
        <h3 class="person-name">PG</h3>
        <p class="person-role">Co-Founder</p>
        <p>PG is a senior software engineer with eight years of experience across cybersecurity, cloud infrastructure, embedded systems, and artificial intelligence. His career spans roles at Broadcom, and Visteon Corporation, where he has worked across software development, infrastructure, security, and production delivery.</p>
        <p>Most recently, PG served as a Staff Software Engineer at Broadcom, where he was part of the core development team responsible for authentication and authorization, security updates, and cloud infrastructure. He helped establish CI/CD processes across multiple microservices and worked across both AWS and Google Cloud environments. During his time at VMware and later Broadcom, he was also responsible for introducing AI into the engineering process, exploring how emerging tools could support software development and delivery.</p>
        <p>Previously, PG worked as a Software Engineer at Visteon Corporation, developing embedded software for automotive systems used by the Volkswagen Group. His work included real-time operating systems, memory management, low-level drivers, software testing, and release delivery. He also contributed to establishing a production process at one of the company’s facilities.</p>
        <p>Across his career, PG has developed technical experience spanning low-level embedded systems, cloud-native infrastructure, cybersecurity, and AI. This breadth has given him a strong understanding of how software is built, secured, tested, and delivered in complex production environments, while continuing to explore how emerging technologies can strengthen the engineering process.</p>
        <p>PG holds a Bachelor’s degree in Software Engineering and a Master’s degree in Artificial Intelligence, with a thesis focused on computer vision for mobile devices. He has also completed Stanford University’s XCS224N course in Natural Language Processing with Deep Learning.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
